From 23d5f557ef133c379d5326fe6f49d2c2a3b29b10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:55:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] client: fixed cause for files that are not regular, one
 warning for many unreadable mails
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

warnCause gives "Datei nicht lesbar" for store.ErrNotRegular, after every
other cause, so only what was "Prüfung fehlgeschlagen" changes (Nr. 104).
unprocessedTerms keeps the local rule only for *fs.PathError
(unreadableCause): warnCause does not know it, as elsewhere it is also an
error of writing or of a directory. The one warning of Read that changes
is "Epochenkette von <id> bricht bei Epoche <n> ab: Datei nicht lesbar."
for an epoch.rec that is not a regular file.

Index and Search collect the mails marked unprocessed that they cannot
read (no verdict on their bytes) and warn when the call ends, also on an
early return: one warning per mail up to nine, from ten on one warning
with their number, the fixed causes and the first five mail IDs; a mail
named by several entries counts once (Nr. 103). Verdicts stay a warning
per mail, at once; Search repeats one on each call until Index has
deleted the marker. Which mails are accepted, which markers are deleted
and the terms are unchanged.

Tests: TestUnprocessedMailEACCES (runs only where a file with mode 000
gives EACCES, else skips with the reason; Nr. 102),
TestUnprocessedUnreadableTogether, TestUnprocessedUnreadableMany (more
than ten mails, the first five in the order met, an early return of
Search) and TestWarnUnreadable (two causes; Nr. 103), TestMailWithTrailer
(a mail file with a signature trailer, which envelope.Parse accepts, is
refused by openMail; Nr. 106), TestUnprocessedMailGrewBeyond (the branch
"grew beyond" of store.ReadFileLimited for a mail file, reached without
a change of package store: a fanotify permission event holds the first
read of the file until it has grown by one byte, so the append does not
race the reader; without CAP_SYS_ADMIN it skips with the reason; Nr.
107), TestTermsAddressesFromRawHeader in internal/ingest (the server
takes from: and to: from the raw header, encoded words with a comma;
Nr. 107), cases in TestWarnCause (store.ErrNotRegular, and after a cause
such as errResign).

Task: docs/tasks/28-nach-m1-nacht2c.md (Paket 28C)
